    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0212" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.A Summaries/9–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Austin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-30T00:50:00-05:00">September 30,
                        1949—12:50 a. m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>1204.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">General Assembly</hi> (230<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">th Plenary</hi>)</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">summary</hi>
                </p>
                <p>By a vote of 45–6 (Yugoslavia, and Soviet bloc)–5 (Afghanistan, Haiti, Israel,
                    Syria, Yemen), the GA Sept. 29 approved the
                        GC recommendation for inclusion in the agenda
                    and allocation to Committee 1<anchor n="1" xml:id="d116-f1"/> of the Chinese
                    charge that the USSR was threatening the <pb facs="0213" n="197" xml:id="pg197"
                    /> political independence and territorial integrity of China and peace in the
                    Far East.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d116-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d116-f1" n="1" xml:id="d116-f1-content">
                <p>The First (Political and Security) Committee of the General Assembly.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d116-f2" n="2" xml:id="d116-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">Official Records</hi>, Plenary Meetings of the
                    General Assembly, 20 September–10 December 1949, p. 95.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
